False news stories spread 6× faster and reach 10× more people on Twitter than true stories, according to a landmark 2018 MIT study in Science — misinformation is more viral, not less.
Algorithmic amplification of outrage-inducing content increases engagement by 20% per unit of moral outrage (Brady et al., 2017, PNAS) — platforms are structurally incentivised to promote divisive content.
The Myanmar genocide (2017) was directly facilitated by Facebook's algorithm amplifying anti-Rohingya hate speech; UN investigators cited Facebook as a 'contributing factor' to the violence.
